The chain (newest last)
-----------------------

1. Reconstruction, Windows + Linux build, H9XASH wiring, DF_admins parity. The decompiled binary was
   rebuilt as nine source modules (util, strutil, beam, entfuncs, dispatch, weaponcore, admintools,
   entmover, dll) plus the Metamod glue, with the H9 layer in src/h9. Builds to Windows (MSBuild) and
   Linux (make). DF_admins.txt admin recognition accepts the h9_clientid Xash id as well as the engine
   auth id / SteamID; _entpass is still the password. (The real DF_admins.txt is gitignored;
   DF_admins.example.txt is the committed template.)

2. HAVOC9 gate. Loaded on every map but inert unless the map name contains "entmap", the map is one of
   the ";"-separated names in the entmod_maps cvar, or the operator set entmod_force 1. The entmod
   cvar is a state readout the gate sets each map (1 = tools live, 0 = inert). While active the server
   de-ranks (no career XP / ELO) through the AMXX entmod_map() gate. The decision is printed to the
   server console each map ("[EntMod] map '<name>' -> tools ON/off").

3. Console-command registration restored. The original registered its commands with the engine; the
   first reconstruction had dropped that and only caught them through the ClientCommand hook, so they
   never showed in the console and were not recognised on a listen server. Every command (e_*, es_*,
   t_*, mm_*, entmod_*, weapon_entmover) registers again, so they appear in the console and run when
   typed. Added entmod_myid, which privately prints a player's own ids so they can be added to
   DF_admins.txt.

4. sv_cheats with the tools. The tools (equipping the entmover, spawning, noclip, giving weapons) are
   cheat-protected, so they did nothing with sv_cheats 0. The gate now sets sv_cheats 1 while the tools
   are live and back to 0 otherwise.

5. weapon_entmover toggles off. Typing weapon_entmover again while the tool is out now holsters it and
   restores the player's real weapon.
